# __APP_NAME__

A Winia application generated by Winia Forge.

## Desktop

```bash
cargo run
```

## Android

`[android].abis` lists every ABI that goes into the APK; the generated project defaults to
`arm64-v8a` and `x86_64`, so one APK runs on both real devices and emulators. Each ABI needs
its Rust target installed (`rustup target add aarch64-linux-android x86_64-linux-android`).

```bash
winia build --target android   # assemble the APK
winia run --target android     # build incrementally, install, and launch
```

`winia build --abi arm64-v8a` narrows the build to a single ABI when a smaller APK is wanted.

`winia build` locates the NDK, injects the linker / `CC` / `AR` environment, copies the
`.so` into `android/app/src/main/jniLibs/<abi>/`, verifies 16 KB alignment, and runs the
Gradle wrapper. It needs the Android SDK/NDK, JDK 17 or 21, LLVM libclang for bindgen, and
Python 3.

Skia's Graphite/wgpu variant has no published prebuilt archive, so the first build compiles Skia
and Dawn from source. Its GN rules invoke `python3` explicitly: `python3 --version` must succeed
on `PATH`. On Windows, `python` alone is not enough; install the `python3` alias or provide a
project-local `python3.cmd` that forwards to `python`.

The generated Android project uses GameActivity. Rendering uses Skia Graphite on wgpu; the old
`vulkan` and `gl` Cargo features have been removed.
